    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation on `POST /api/owners`. When a create is retried with an `Idempotency-Key` header that was already seen, the endpoint now returns the originally created owner with **200 OK** instead of creating a duplicate (which the household/duplicate rules would otherwise reject with 409).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `Idempotency-Key` header parameter (optional) and a `200` response to the `addOwner` operation. This is the idiomatic route here since the request-mapping interface (`OwnersApi`) is generated by the openapi-generator plugin from this spec; regenerating produces an `addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto, @RequestHeader(\"Idempotency-Key\") String)` method with a standard `@RequestHeader`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the `addOwner` override to the new signature and added the idempotency logic:\n   - A `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` remembers, per key, the id of the owner it originally created.\n   - On a request carrying a known key, it fetches and returns that owner with 200.\n   - Otherwise it runs the normal `createNewOwner` pipeline (all existing validation/quota/household rules untouched) and, only on a successful `201`, records the key \u2192 new owner id.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `coreIdempotentRepeat` acceptance test), `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne design note worth surfacing: the idempotency store is in-memory and lives for the application's lifetime (fine for the single-instance test/spec here), so it isn't shared across instances or persisted across restarts. If you later need cross-instance idempotency, this would move to a persistent/shared store.",
