    "probe_text": "Here is every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. The endpoint is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `createNewOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\n## Before the controller runs\n\n1. **Spring Security filter chain** \u2014 authenticates the request. Two mutually exclusive chains selected by `petclinic.security.enable` (`BasicAuthenticationConfig` = HTTP Basic + JDBC users when `true`; `DisableSecurityConfig` = permit-all when `false`).\n2. **Bean Validation of the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, from the generated `OwnersApi`). Failure \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Field constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 optional, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `email` \u2014 optional, `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional, `@Size(4..4)`\n   - `title`, `sharesHousehold`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 no constraints\n3. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. Failure \u2192 **403**.\n\n## Inside the controller\n\n4. **Idempotency replay check** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before (in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`) and the owner still exists, return the existing owner as **200** (no new creation).\n5. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping** (MapStruct `OwnerMapper.toOwner`); `id`/`pets` ignored, `sharesHousehold` read separately.\n\n**`normalizeNewOwner` \u2014 in-place normalization + validation (any failure \u2192 400):**\n\n6. **Address normalization** \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, else the flat `address`; trims, collapses whitespace, uppercases, expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE). If no address present \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`Telephones.toE164`) \u2014 strips separators, applies `+61` default (dropping leading 0), requires 8\u201315 digits plus per-country national-length rules (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Email** \u2014 lowercased; rejected if domain is disposable (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**.\n9. **Postcode locality check** \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits and within the region range for its locality (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Mismatch \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Registration date** \u2014 null defaults to today; a future date \u2192 **400**; otherwise rolled forward past weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays to the next business day.\n\n**Capacity gates:**\n\n11. **Daily limit** \u2014 \u2265100 existing owners with the same registration date \u2192 **429**.\n12. **City capacity** \u2014 \u226550 existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409**.\n\n**Household resolution:**\n\n13. **Compute `householdId`** \u2014 SHA-256 of normalized last name + `|` + postcode (first 12 hex chars).\n14. **Household-duplicate gate** \u2014 if an existing owner shares last name + postcode and the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**Derived-attribute assignment (`assignDerivedAttributes`, order matters):**\n\n15. **`customerCode`** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` from telephone+lastName; suffixed `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 on collision to stay unique.\n16. **`namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n17. **`membershipNumber`** \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from registration fiscal year.\n18. **`bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 true if >80 existing owners share the registration date.\n19. **`householdSize`** \u2014 count of existing owners with same `householdId`, +1.\n20. **`possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 if not a declared household member, flags the lowest-id owner with same last name + postcode but different telephone.\n\n**Persist and finish:**\n\n21. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional` JPA insert via Spring Data (`IDENTITY`-generated id). No re-validation or defaulting here.\n22. **Audit log** \u2014 INFO line to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n23. **Map to `OwnerDto`** (computing transient read-only fields), **store the idempotency-key \u2192 id mapping**, and return **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n## Notably absent\n\n- **No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist` or entity lifecycle callbacks** \u2014 all derivation is imperative in the controller.\n- **No `@EventListener`/`ApplicationEvent`** \u2014 nothing reacts to creation via events.\n- **No emails or external notifications** \u2014 the AUDIT log is the only notification.\n- The `Owner`/`Person` **entity-level** constraints (`@NotEmpty`, E.164 `@Pattern`, `@Email`) do **not** fire on this path, because the controller binds and validates the DTO, not the entity, and `saveOwner` performs no revalidation."
